  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Solar Midwives and Families</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Over 50% of Mayan children living in the Western Highlands of Guatemala are severely malnourished. The children grow up stunted, never to reach their potential height and their brains don&apos;t develop properly. This locks them in severe generational poverty. Solar power and water filters save families in remote villages ~ $5.50 per week that they once spent on candles. Families spend their extra income on better nutrition to their children.  With solar lights kids study at night for the first time.</narrative>
  </description>
